WEBVTT

00:00:00.706 --> 00:00:05.086
One agent is useful. Several at once is where FlightDeck shines.

00:00:05.086 --> 00:00:11.109
Every agent gets its own branch and its own worktree, so they never edit the same files.

00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:14.111
The first agent adds a dark theme.

00:00:26.299 --> 00:00:29.673
While it works, start a second agent, for search.

00:00:29.673 --> 00:00:32.290
Tell it to leave the stylesheet alone:

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.287
that's the first agent's job.

00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:46.848
And a third, to rewrite the README.

00:00:58.964 --> 00:01:01.795
Now three agents are working at once.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:05.698
The sidebar shows each one's state, and its branch.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:11.659
Switch between them with Option and a number, or a click, to watch one or steer it.

00:01:12.751 --> 00:01:18.227
All three are done, each on its own branch, with its work committed.

00:01:18.227 --> 00:01:21.528
Finish merges them into main, one by one.

00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:42.582
Three features, built side by side in the time of one, and all of them merged into main.
